<title>POLAND: Polish net reserves rise to $21.81 bln in 1996.</title>
<headline>Polish net reserves rise to $21.81 bln in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish net foreign currency reserves grew by $350 million in December 1996 to $21.81 billion and were $1.37 billion higher than in December 1995, the National Bank of Poland said. </p>
<p>    POLISH RESERVES (bln dollars)   DEC 96	NOV 96     DEC 95</p>
<p>    Official reserves		  NA	  17.85	14.96</p>
<p>    Net reserves		     21.81	 21.46	20.44</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures in billions of dollars. Official reserves are those held by the state. Net reserves mean the total amount of hard currencies in the whole banking system.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
